course: dictionary
lesson: 8856
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things in different sentences. Shook is the past tense of shake, so it can mean moved quickly up and down, trembled, upset someone, or greeted someone. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «The earthquake shook the town.» Here the ground was moving, so shook means moved quickly up and down or side to side. «Her hands shook as she opened the letter.» Here her hands trembled, so shook means trembled with fear. Ask yourself: what is moving, and why?
explain: Shook also appears in set phrases. «Mr Wilson shook his hand» means he greeted him or agreed with him. «She shook her head» means she moved her head side to side to say no. Learn phrases like these as a group of words, not one word at a time.
explain: Shook can be slang in American English, meaning scared or upset. This is informal, so you will mostly meet it in chatty talk, not in school books. When you are not sure, read the clues and check a dictionary.
fact: Shook is the past tense of the verb shake.
fact: «The news shook us» means the news upset or shocked us.
fact: «Shook hands» means took someone's hand to greet them or to agree.
fact: «Shook his head» means moved his head from side to side to say no.
fact: Shook can also mean trembled, as with fear or cold, or be slang in American English meaning scared or upset.
exercise: «The ground shook during the earthquake.» What does shook mean here? | *Moved quickly up and down or side to side | Was very quiet | Ate a big meal | Greeted someone warmly
exercise: «Mr Wilson shook his hand.» What does shook mean here? | Trembled with cold | Dropped it on the floor | *Greeted him, or agreed with him | Hid it in a pocket
exercise: «Her voice shook as she told the story.» What does shook mean? | Whispered in secret | *Trembled, as with fear or nerves | Spoke very loudly | Sang happily
test: «He shook his head.» What does this show? | He said yes | He hit his head on the door | He lifted his head to look up | *He moved his head side to side to say no
test: «The news shook us all.» What does shook mean? | *Upset or shocked us | Woke us up gently | Moved us to a new house | Made us laugh a lot
exam: «Every time a box shook and glowed before opening, his heart jumped.» What does shook mean in this sentence? | Melted slowly in the sun | Was empty and quiet | Greeted someone warmly | *Rattled, moving quickly up and down or side to side
